# The release image ships the frontend bundle, so this one dist is committed. deploy/Dockerfile.release
# opens with "Integrator supplies reviewed C source and A's already built frontend/dist" and runs
# `release_check --profile integrated` at build time, which fails without those files. Render builds
# from git, so an ignored dist makes the release image unbuildable. Committing it also makes
# staleness visible: after a frontend change, `git status` shows the rebuilt bundle instead of hiding it.
!matchmind/frontend/dist/
